        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_SINK1 : J2.1(Pin_1,passive) R32.1(passive) SW7.8(passive) U22.1(/OE,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_SINK2 : J13.1(Pin_1,passive) R4.1(passive) SW7.7(passive) U15.1(/OE,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) R60.2(passive) U36.4(Y,output)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "acorn-motherboard:SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | pins: 1=/OE(input) 2=A(input) 3=GND(power_in) 4=Y(output) 5=VCC(power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Safety/e-stop: an e-stop loop with multiple sink points (ESTOP_SINK1, ESTOP_SINK2, ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL) gated through single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is what gets assembled, the outputs can actively drive high where the intended open-drain devices would release the sink lines. This can cause contention or prevent the e-stop sink chain from behaving as intended, compromising the fail-safe e-stop interface.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomaly detected: the e-stop buffers are specified as open-drain SN74LVC1G07 devices, but the sourcing metadata names push-pull U74LVC1G125 parts. Substituting the listed parts can change the e-stop sink behavior and undermine its fail-safe operation."
}

